  "configuration_id": "config_033",
  "reason": "The current best is config_032 (multimodal, multiprofile, scVI_n200, ResNet50, transformer, concat) at 0.688 accuracy. The strongest evidence shows that scVI_n200 + multiprofile + transformer aggregation is the optimal RNA backbone, and adding ResNet50 image features with concat fusion improved over RNA-only by ~3.5%. The key uncertainty is whether the fusion strategy can be further optimized: weighted fusion allows the model to learn modality-specific importance weights rather than treating both branches equally via concatenation. Config_033 changes only the fusion method (concat → weighted) while holding all other settings identical to config_032, making it a clean single-variable ablation. With only 2 experiments remaining after this one, isolating the fusion effect is the highest-value exploitation step: if weighted fusion improves accuracy, it directly upgrades our best configuration; if not, we confirm concat is sufficient and can use the final experiments to explore the image encoder (ViT-L) as the remaining lever."
}

